No, 6 Larch Grove is not in a conservation area. Our records also show it is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

The constraints check returned no conservation area designation (the field came back empty), so I'd suggest confirming that with the council if it matters for your plans.

On the windows, the council guidance says replacement windows only need an application in a conservation area if they don't match the existing windows in material and pattern. Since 6 Larch Grove isn't in a conservation area, that particular requirement doesn't apply to you on the information I have.

I can't see the attached photo in this conversation, so I can't comment on the windows themselves. I also can't give a formal planning opinion. If you're unsure whether your specific works need permission, the council can confirm that. If you tell me the proposed changes, such as a change in size, number of windows, or a different opening style, I can check the guidance for those too.
